<https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-sn> a owl:Ontology ;
    dct:title "SCORM 2004 4th Edition — Sequencing and Navigation (IMS Simple Sequencing and ADL extensions)"@en ;
    dct:description "An OWL 2 DL ontology and SHACL shapes for the sequencing definitions of SCORM 2004 4th Edition: IMS Simple Sequencing 1.0 as SCORM applies it — sequencing definitions and collections, control modes, pre-, exit- and post-condition rules with their conditions and actions, limit conditions, rollup rules, objectives with their global-objective maps, randomization and delivery controls, auxiliary resources — and ADL's extensions: rollup and constrained-choice considerations, objectivesGlobalToSystem, the 4th Edition's extended objective maps (raw, minimum and maximum score, completion status, progress measure), and the navigation presentation that hides LMS controls. It imports the content-packaging ontology, whose items and organizations carry the sequencing."@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Independent formalization by Mark Spivey (Foxxi Mediums Inc.). Not affiliated with or endorsed by ADL or 1EdTech. Where this document and the published standard differ, the standard governs."@en ,
        "Transcribed from the normative schema: imsss_v1p0.xsd and the schemas it includes (IMS Simple Sequencing 1.0), adlseq_v1p3.xsd and adlnav_v1p3.xsd, as distributed with SCORM 2004 4th Edition."@en ,
        "Since 2026.10.0: adlObjective relates a sequencing definition to the 4th Edition's adlseq:objective, in place of adlObjectives, which pointed at the imsss Objectives class and is deprecated; presentation is the item's, not the sequencing definition's, and objectivesGlobalToSystem the organization's — both without a domain, so that data written with the earlier reading stays consistent."@en ,
        "An instance written as JSON is read into this ontology through the JSON-LD 1.1 context published at https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-sn/context/2026.10.0, which is generated from this document. The shapes at https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-sn/shapes/2026.10.0 constrain that reading, and the Foxxi validator (POST https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-sn/validate) checks the JSON against the same shapes."@en ,
        "The shapes select a node by its class (sh:targetClass) and, as the RDFS domain and range rules make a node an instance of a class, by a property it has (sh:targetSubjectsOf) or by the property that reaches it (sh:targetObjectsOf): a node is checked whether or not it declares its type. The Foxxi validator selects the same nodes of the JSON, and every result cites its shape."@en ,
        "Earlier publications served this document's terms under https://interego-foxxi-bridge.livelysky-8b81abb0.eastus.azurecontainerapps.io/ns/scorm-sn#, on a host since retired. A term IRI in that namespace names the term with the same local name in this one; the Foxxi validator reads it so, and nothing is published there any more."@en ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://foxxi-bridge.interego.xwisee.com/ns/scorm-sn/2026.10.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "2026.10.0" ;
    skos:historyNote "Versioned by calendar (YYYY.MM.PATCH) from 2026.10.0: the version numbers this document, not the standard it formalizes. Every released version stays resolvable at its version IRI, and the content there never changes. Earlier publications carried no version IRI, and their owl:versionInfo restated the version of the standard."@en ;
